We come out of the badminton club.
There is a tea stall nearby.
We walk there.
Amit says to the tea vendor, "Dada, give four cutting chais."
Dada gives us hot tea.
We all take the glasses of tea in our hands.
Neha looks at me and smiles.
She says, "Maya, we are good friends now."
"Let's call each other 'tu' instead of 'tumhi' now."
Sanjay laughs and says, "Yes, definitely!"
Then Amit asks me, "Maya, when did you come to Mumbai?"
I say, "I came to Mumbai in January."
Sanjay asks curiously, "Why did you come this far from Mexico?"
I answer, "I got a job in a software company here."
"That is why I came to India."
Neha asks, "When you first came here, what all happened?"
I remember those first days in January.
I take a sip of tea and tell them my story.
